  "articleBody": "You might be surprised how many bedroom safety upgrades you can tackle yourself, but there are definitely times when bringing in a professional is not just helpful, but necessary. If you're thinking about changing the height of your bed in a way that affects transfers, especially for someone with mobility challenges, a pro can ensure it's done safely. Another big one is anything involving ceiling-mounted lifting systems; these absolutely require expert installation to prevent serious accidents. And if your safety upgrades involve integrated electrical work or changes to the structural components of your walls, like adding support for grab bars or modifying built-ins, you'll want a qualified contractor. They can handle permits and make sure everything meets code, which is super important. An occupational therapist can also be invaluable in assessing the user's specific functional needs and making sure the modifications truly fit their lifestyle. Don't hesitate to reach out for help when the job gets complex or involves anything structural or electrical; it's always better to be safe than sorry!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}